der:1px solid rgba(52,211,153,.22);border-radius:10px;padding:13px;\"><div style=\"font-size:11px;color:#34d399;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:6px;\">Base Case</div><div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#e2e8f0;\">Treat the 8:30 BEA data and clustered 10:00 releases as volatility checkpoints. Let the opening range form; respect the overnight range and auction/SCOOS timing, and require price acceptance before extending a move.</div></div><div style=\"background:rgba(248,113,113,.07);border:1px solid rgba(248,113,113,.22);border-radius:10px;padding:13px;\"><div style=\"font-size:11px;color:#f87171;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:6px;\">Invalidation</div><div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#e2e8f0;\">Invalidate a range/fade bias on sustained ES acceptance outside the overnight range, especially if Treasury yields and MOVE extend higher together. Reassess around 2:00 PM SCOOS; no directional forecast is implied.</div></div></div></section>"}